            <div xml:id="d310">

                <pb facs="0460" n="342" sameAs="frus:frus1928v02/pg342"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">493.11 N 15/136: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >MacMurray</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-05-02T18:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 2, 1928—6
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>141. Your 290, April 30, 4 p.m. Secretaries of Presbyterian Board decline to act
                    before Board meeting May 14. Department believes Board might then be persuaded
                    to assent but recommends that under the circumstances you endeavor to find and
                    appoint some one else. Department suggests for your consideration Frank S.
                    Williams, Registrar of China Trade Act,<anchor n="23" xml:id="d310-f1"/> but
                    leaves choice to you.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d310-f1" n="23" xml:id="d310-f1-content">
                <p>Act approved Sept. 19, 1922 (42 Stat. 849).</p>
            </note>
